  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly ends the phrase “Until next time” with an exclamation mark, but the existing noun-ending period rule overwhelms the weak generic exclamation output. A suffix rule for that reusable phrase raises the appropriate punctuation without removing alternatives. Newline targets occur after several kinds of opening noun phrases and after action sentences ending in a period; the added rules cover those POS-level patterns rather than memorizing complete documents. The period rule could also match a sentence that is final, so the competing end-token option is deliberately retained. The remaining “One morning,” example supports a narrow temporal-introductory comma rule. These are provisional batch-driven repairs; replay behavior and mean loss still require the replay gate."
